COMMENT ON TABLE vendor.invoice IS 'Invoice, reconciliation, and billing resolution record for media vendors, publishers, and production suppliers. Captures the full invoice-to-payment lifecycle: invoice receipt (number, vendor reference, billing period, gross/net amounts, currency, payment due date), reconciliation against IO-authorized spend and actual ad server delivery data (CM360, The Trade Desk) including variance amount, variance percentage, discrepancy reason code, reconciliation period, dispute management, resolution status, and final approved billing amount. Supports invoice statuses: received, reconciled, approved, disputed, paid. Feeds SAP S/4HANA Accounts Payable, Mediaocean Prisma post-buy reconciliation, and financial close processes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.invoice_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for the invoice record in the vendor billing and reconciliation system. Primary key for the invoice data product within the vendor domain.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Advertising invoices are typically allocated to specific client brands, not just advertiser level. Brand-level budget tracking and P&L reporting require invoice-to-brand attribution. Essential for bra LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the advertising campaign associated with the media spend or production services billed on this invoice. Enables campaign-level financial reconciliation and P&L reporting. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: Vendor invoices in media buying are issued against specific insertion orders. Linking invoice.contract_insertion_order_id enables IO-to-invoice matching, authorized spend validation, and payment appro LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: Invoices often bill at flight level in multi-flight campaigns for granular financial tracking. Essential for flight-level budget reconciliation, variance analysis, and financial reporting in advertisi LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.flight.flight_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Vendor invoices must be allocated to projects/initiatives for accurate project cost accounting, budget tracking, and financial reporting. Essential for project P&L, variance analysis, and client billi LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.line_item_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.line_item. Business justification: Invoices frequently itemize by line item for granular billing and cost tracking. Critical for line-item-level cost reconciliation, variance analysis, and financial reporting in advertising media buyin LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.line_item.line_item_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.production_job_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.production_job. Business justification: Accounts payable / production cost reconciliation: vendor invoices for studio, post-production, and talent services must be matched to the production job they bill against. Finance teams reconcile act LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.production_job.production_job_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Vendor invoices often bill against SOW-level budgets and scope, not just insertion orders. Finance teams reconcile invoice amounts to SOW committed spend and track SOW budget burn rates across multipl LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.supplier_id IS 'Reference to the third-party media vendor, publisher, technology partner (DSP/SSP/DMP), or production supplier who issued this invoice. Links to the vendor master record. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.agency_discount_amount IS 'The monetary value of agency commission or trade discount deducted from the gross invoice amount, as negotiated in the vendor contract or IO. Typically expressed as a percentage of gross media spend.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.approved_billing_amount IS 'The final approved amount authorized for payment after reconciliation and dispute resolution. May differ from the original net_amount if adjustments were made during the reconciliation or dispute process. This is the amount posted to SAP S/4HANA FI-AP for payment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.billing_period_end IS 'The end date of the media flight, production period, or service period covered by this invoice. Together with billing_period_start, defines the reconciliation window for delivery data matching.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.billing_period_start IS 'The start date of the media flight, production period, or service period covered by this invoice. Used to align invoice charges with campaign delivery windows and IO-authorized spend periods.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.brand_safety_compliant IS 'Indicates whether the media inventory delivered by the vendor during the billing period was verified as brand-safe per TAG (Trustworthy Accountability Group) and internal brand safety standards. A value of False may trigger invoice dispute or vendor review.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary amounts on this invoice (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR). Required for multi-currency media buying operations and SAP S/4HANA foreign currency revaluation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.delivered_spend_amount IS 'The actual ad spend amount as recorded by the ad server (Google CM360) or DSP (The Trade Desk) for the billing period. Represents the verified delivery data used in post-buy reconciliation against the vendor invoice.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.delivery_data_source IS 'The ad server or measurement platform used as the authoritative source of delivery data for reconciliation (e.g., Google CM360, The Trade Desk). Determines which system''s impression and spend data is used to validate the vendor invoice. Code set: ref.delivery_data_source.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.discrepancy_reason_code IS 'Standardized code identifying the root cause of the reconciliation variance. Delivery shortfall: vendor delivered less than invoiced. Overbilling: vendor charged above IO rate. Trafficking error: ad server setup error. Invalid traffic: IVT/fraud detected. Make good: compensatory delivery. Code set: ref.discrepancy_reason_code.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.dispute_raised_date IS 'The date on which a formal billing dispute was raised with the vendor. Initiates the dispute resolution clock and triggers vendor notification per contractual SLA terms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.dispute_resolution_date IS 'The date on which the billing dispute was formally resolved and the approved billing amount was agreed upon with the vendor. Marks the transition from ''disputed'' to ''approved'' status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.dispute_resolution_notes IS 'Free-text narrative documenting the outcome of the dispute resolution process, including the agreed adjustment, vendor concessions, make-good arrangements, or credit note details.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.gross_amount IS 'The total gross amount billed by the vendor before any agency discounts, rebates, or adjustments. Represents the full rate card value of media or services delivered as stated on the vendor invoice.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.invalid_traffic_flag IS 'Indicates whether invalid traffic (IVT) or ad fraud was detected in the delivery data for this invoice period, as identified by TAG-certified measurement tools. A True value triggers discrepancy_reason_code = ''invalid_traffic'' and initiates dispute proceedings.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.invoice_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the invoice within the invoice-to-payment workflow. Received: invoice has been received from vendor. Reconciled: matched against IO and delivery data. Approved: cleared for payment. Disputed: discrepancy identified requiring resolution. Paid: payment has been issued.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.invoice_type IS 'Classification of the invoice by the nature of services billed. Media covers ad placements and programmatic buys; production covers creative and content production; technology covers DSP/SSP/DMP platform fees; data covers audience data and analytics services; talent covers freelance and contractor services. Code set: ref.invoice_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.io_authorized_amount IS 'The total spend amount authorized under the associated Insertion Order (IO) for the billing period. Used as the baseline for reconciliation against the vendor invoice gross amount to identify overbilling or underbilling.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.issue_date IS 'The date the invoice was issued by the vendor, as stated on the invoice document. Used as the principal business event date for the invoice and for payment terms calculation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.net_amount IS 'The net payable amount after deducting agency discounts and rebates from the gross amount. This is the amount recorded in SAP S/4HANA Accounts Payable for payment processing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.number IS 'Externally-assigned invoice number as provided by the vendor on the invoice document. Used as the primary business identifier for matching vendor invoices to internal purchase orders and IOs. Must be unique per vendor.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.payment_date IS 'The date on which payment was issued to the vendor for the approved billing amount. Populated when invoice status transitions to ''paid''. Used for cash flow reporting and vendor payment history.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.payment_due_date IS 'The contractual date by which payment must be made to the vendor to comply with agreed payment terms (e.g., Net 30, Net 60). Used for cash flow planning and avoiding late payment penalties.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.payment_reference IS 'The payment transaction reference number generated by SAP S/4HANA FI-AP when the payment run is executed. Used to trace the payment in bank statements and vendor remittance advice.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.payment_terms IS 'The contractual payment terms agreed with the vendor, defining the number of days from invoice receipt to payment due date (e.g., Net 30, Net 60). Sourced from the vendor contract in SAP S/4HANA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.received_date IS 'The date the invoice was received and logged into the accounts payable system. May differ from the issue date due to postal or electronic delivery lag. Used for aging analysis and payment terms compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.reconciliation_date IS 'The date on which the invoice reconciliation was completed and the variance amount and percentage were calculated. Marks the transition from ''received'' to ''reconciled'' status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.reconciliation_period_end IS 'The end date of the reconciliation window used to pull delivery data from CM360 or The Trade Desk for matching against this invoice.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.reconciliation_period_start IS 'The start date of the reconciliation window used to pull delivery data from CM360 or The Trade Desk for matching against this invoice. May differ from billing_period_start if reconciliation covers a different date range.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.tax_amount IS 'The applicable tax amount (e.g., VAT, GST, sales tax) charged on the invoice as required by the vendor''s jurisdiction. Recorded separately for tax compliance and SAP S/4HANA FI tax reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.total_payable_amount IS 'The final total amount payable to the vendor, calculated as net_amount plus tax_amount. This is the amount that will be disbursed in the payment run in SAP S/4HANA FI-AP.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.variance_amount IS 'The monetary difference between the vendor''s invoiced gross amount and the delivered spend amount recorded by the ad server or DSP. A positive value indicates overbilling by the vendor; negative indicates underbilling.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.variance_percentage IS 'The variance amount expressed as a percentage of the delivered spend amount. Used to assess whether the discrepancy exceeds the industry-standard tolerance threshold (typically 10% per MRC guidelines) triggering a formal dispute.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.invoice.vendor_reference_number IS 'Vendor''s own internal reference or purchase order number included on the invoice, used to cross-reference the vendor''s billing system and facilitate dispute resolution.';
