COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.vendor_io_media_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key reference to the parent Insertion Order header that this line item belongs to. Satisfies TRANSACTION_LINE HEADER_REFERENCE category — mandatory link to the parent IO. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_insertion_order.media_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.vendor_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.vendor_rate_card. Business justification: Each io_line represents a discrete media buy priced against a vendor''s published rate card. The io_line carries rate fields (rate, net_rate, agency_commission_pct, ad_format, ad_unit_size) that are de LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.vendor_rate_card.vendor_rate_card_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.actual_spend IS 'The actual amount spent against this line item based on delivered units and applicable rate, as reported by the vendor or ad server. Compared against contracted_spend during financial reconciliation in Mediaocean Prisma and SAP S/4HANA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.actual_units_delivered IS 'The actual number of units (impressions, clicks, GRPs, etc.) delivered by the vendor for this line item as reported by the ad server or third-party measurement provider. Used in reconciliation against contracted_units to identify under- or over-delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.added_value_flag IS 'Indicates whether this line item represents added-value inventory (bonus impressions, editorial mentions, or complimentary placements) provided by the vendor at no additional cost as part of the negotiated IO package.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.agency_commission_pct IS 'The agency commission percentage applied to this line item''s gross spend, typically 15% per industry standard. Used to calculate net vendor cost and agency revenue. Expressed as a percentage (e.g., 15.00 for 15%).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.brand_safety_segments IS 'Comma-separated list of brand safety and content suitability categories applied to this line item to prevent ad adjacency with inappropriate content. Aligned with TAG Brand Safety Standards and IAB Content Taxonomy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.buying_type IS 'The pricing and buying model for this line item. Specifies whether inventory is purchased on a Cost Per Mille (CPM), Cost Per Click (CPC), Cost Per Acquisition (CPA), Cost Per View (CPV), Cost Per Completed View (CPCV), flat rate, Gross Rating Point (GRP), or Target Rating Point (TRP) basis. Code set: ref.buying_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.contracted_spend IS 'The total authorized spend amount for this line item as agreed in the Insertion Order (rate × contracted_units for unit-based buys, or flat rate for flat buys). Represents the financial commitment to the vendor. Core to Mediaocean Prisma billing and budget management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.contracted_units IS 'The total number of units (impressions, clicks, acquisitions, GRPs, TRPs, or views) contracted with the vendor for this line item as specified in the Insertion Order. Satisfies TRANSACTION_LINE LINE_QUANTITY category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code applicable to all monetary values on this line item (rate, contracted spend, actual spend). Supports multi-currency media buying across international campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.delivery_method IS 'The mechanism by which ad inventory is purchased and delivered for this line item. Distinguishes between Real-Time Bidding (RTB) programmatic, programmatic direct, guaranteed direct buys, non-guaranteed direct, and Private Marketplace (PMP) deals. Core to The Trade Desk and Mediaocean Prisma workflow classification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.dsp_line_code IS 'The external line item identifier assigned by the Demand-Side Platform (DSP), such as The Trade Desk, for programmatic buys. Enables cross-system reconciliation between Mediaocean Prisma and the DSP platform.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.flight_end_date IS 'The date on which ad delivery for this line item is scheduled to end. Defines the close of the contracted flight period. Used for campaign scheduling, pacing, and vendor reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.flight_start_date IS 'The date on which ad delivery for this line item is scheduled to begin. Defines the start of the contracted flight period. Used for campaign scheduling, pacing, and reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.frequency_cap IS 'Maximum number of times a unique user or household may be served an ad from this line item within the frequency_cap_period. Controls ad fatigue and audience experience as configured in Google Campaign Manager 360 or The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.frequency_cap_period IS 'The time window over which the frequency_cap applies. Defines whether the cap is enforced per hour, day, week, month, or over the lifetime of the campaign flight.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.geo_targeting IS 'Geographic scope of ad delivery for this line item, specifying targeted countries, regions, DMAs, or cities. Expressed as a comma-separated list of location identifiers or descriptive text (e.g., ''USA - New York DMA, Los Angeles DMA'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.grp_contracted IS 'The total Gross Rating Points (GRPs) contracted for this line item, applicable to broadcast, OOH, and audience-guaranteed buys. Represents reach × frequency for the target audience. Tracked via Nielsen Ad Intel.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.line_description IS 'Human-readable description of the media buy represented by this line item, including placement name, ad unit, and targeting summary as specified in the Insertion Order.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.line_number IS 'Sequential line number identifying the position of this line item within the parent Insertion Order. Satisfies TRANSACTION_LINE LINE_SEQUENCE category. Used for ordering, referencing, and reconciliation against vendor invoices.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.line_status IS 'Current workflow and lifecycle status of this IO line item within Mediaocean Prisma. Tracks progression from draft through approval, active delivery, completion, and financial reconciliation. Code set: ref.line_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.makegood_flag IS 'Indicates whether this IO line item is a make-good — compensatory inventory provided by the vendor to offset under-delivery or quality failures on a prior line item. True if this is a make-good line; False otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.net_rate IS 'The net unit rate payable to the vendor after deducting agency commission from the gross rate. Used for vendor invoice validation and SAP S/4HANA accounts payable processing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.prisma_line_code IS 'The native line item identifier from Mediaocean Prisma, the system of record for media planning, buying, billing, and reconciliation. Used for cross-system traceability and audit.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.rate IS 'The negotiated unit rate for this line item expressed in the currency of the IO. Interpretation depends on buying_type: CPM rate per 1,000 impressions, CPC rate per click, CPA rate per acquisition, flat rate for the full flight, or GRP/TRP rate per rating point. Satisfies TRANSACTION_LINE LINE_VALUE_OR_RESULT category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.reconciliation_status IS 'Financial reconciliation status of this line item comparing contracted delivery against vendor-reported actuals. Tracks whether the line has been reconciled, is under dispute, or has been written off. Core to Mediaocean Prisma billing reconciliation workflow.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.targeting_description IS 'Free-text description of the audience targeting parameters applied to this line item, including demographic, geographic, behavioral, contextual, or keyword targeting criteria as configured in The Trade Desk or Google Campaign Manager 360.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.trp_contracted IS 'The total Target Rating Points (TRPs) contracted for this line item, representing GRPs delivered specifically to the defined target audience demographic. Used for audience-guaranteed buys tracked via Nielsen Ad Intel.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.viewability_target_pct IS 'The contracted minimum viewability rate (percentage of served impressions that meet MRC viewability standards) for this line item. Used to enforce quality guarantees with vendors and measure delivery compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.io_line.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
