COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Vendor performance evaluations are often scoped to specific projects they supported, assessing delivery, quality, and responsiveness within project context. Enables project-based vendor scorecarding a LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.production_job_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.production_job. Business justification: Vendor performance management: evaluating a production studio or creative vendor requires referencing the specific production job(s) assessed. Scorecard ratings for delivery fulfillment, revision coun LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.production_job.production_job_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.sla_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sla. Business justification: Vendor performance evaluations directly measure SLA compliance (performance_evaluation has sla_breaches_count, sla_incidents_total, response_time_sla_adherence_rate). Linking to the specific SLA being LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sla.sla_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Performance evaluations assess vendor delivery against SOW scope, deliverables, and SLA targets. Account teams score vendors on SOW fulfillment rates, link evaluation outcomes to SOW renewal decisions LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.supplier_id IS 'Reference to the vendor being evaluated. Links to the vendor master record in the vendor domain. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.actual_delivered_units IS 'Total number of impressions, clicks, or deliverable units actually delivered by the vendor during the evaluation period as recorded in the ad server (e.g., Google Campaign Manager 360). Numerator for delivery fulfillment rate calculation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the senior stakeholder (e.g., VP of Media, Chief Procurement Officer) who formally approved this vendor performance evaluation and its resulting tier assignment and renewal recommendation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.approved_timestamp IS 'Date and time when the vendor performance evaluation was formally approved by the designated approver. Distinct lifecycle event from evaluation completion.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.brand_safety_incident_count IS 'Number of brand safety incidents recorded against the vendor during the evaluation period, including ad placements adjacent to harmful, inappropriate, or non-brand-safe content. Critical metric for TAG (Trustworthy Accountability Group) compliance and preferred vendor list eligibility.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.brand_safety_incident_severity IS 'Highest severity level of brand safety incidents recorded against the vendor during the evaluation period. Aligned to GARM (Global Alliance for Responsible Media) brand safety floor and suitability framework tiers.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.contract_renewal_recommendation IS 'Formal recommendation for contract renewal action based on the outcome of this performance evaluation. Feeds directly into the contract management workflow and vendor relationship strategy decisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.delivery_fulfillment_rate IS 'Percentage of Insertion Order (IO) committed impressions, units, or deliverables that were actually fulfilled by the vendor during the evaluation period. Calculated as (actual_delivered / io_committed) * 100. Core KPI for media vendor accountability.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.disputed_invoices_count IS 'Number of invoices submitted by the vendor during the evaluation period that required dispute resolution, credit notes, or correction due to billing inaccuracies. Feeds into invoice accuracy rate and financial risk assessment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.evaluation_cycle IS 'The fiscal quarter in which this evaluation was conducted, aligned to the QBR (Quarterly Business Review) cycle. Used to track cadence and trend analysis across periods.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.evaluation_date IS 'The principal business date on which the formal vendor performance evaluation was conducted or finalized, typically the QBR session date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.evaluation_notes IS 'Free-text qualitative commentary from the evaluator capturing context, mitigating factors, notable incidents, or strategic observations not captured in the quantitative scorecard metrics. Used in QBR presentations and vendor relationship management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.evaluation_number IS 'Externally-visible business identifier for this evaluation record, used in QBR documentation, vendor communications, and preferred vendor list reviews. Format: VPE-{YEAR}-{SEQUENCE}.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.evaluation_period_end_date IS 'End date of the performance measurement period covered by this evaluation, typically aligned to the quarterly QBR cycle (e.g., last day of the quarter).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.evaluation_period_start_date IS 'Start date of the performance measurement period covered by this evaluation, typically aligned to the quarterly QBR cycle (e.g., first day of the quarter).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.evaluation_status IS 'Current lifecycle state of the vendor performance evaluation record. Draft indicates data collection in progress; in_review indicates pending stakeholder sign-off; completed indicates finalized; approved indicates accepted by vendor management; disputed indicates vendor has raised a formal objection.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.evaluation_year IS 'The fiscal year in which this evaluation was conducted. Combined with evaluation_cycle to uniquely identify the QBR period for trend and year-over-year comparison.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.evaluator_name IS 'Name of the internal agency staff member or team lead responsible for conducting and submitting this vendor performance evaluation, typically the media buyer, account director, or vendor management lead.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.invalid_traffic_rate IS 'Percentage of impressions delivered by the vendor during the evaluation period classified as invalid traffic (IVT) including general invalid traffic (GIVT) and sophisticated invalid traffic (SIVT) per MRC and TAG standards. Critical for fraud prevention and supply chain transparency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.invoice_accuracy_rate IS 'Percentage of vendor invoices submitted during the evaluation period that matched the reconciled billing amounts within the agreed tolerance threshold, without requiring correction or credit notes. Calculated as (accurate_invoices / total_invoices) * 100. Sourced from Mediaocean Prisma reconciliation data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.io_committed_units IS 'Total number of impressions, clicks, or deliverable units committed by the vendor across all active Insertion Orders (IOs) during the evaluation period. Denominator for delivery fulfillment rate calculation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.makegood_fulfilled_count IS 'Number of make-good obligations that were successfully fulfilled by the vendor during the evaluation period. Compared against makegood_obligation_count to assess vendor responsiveness to under-delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.makegood_obligation_count IS 'Number of make-good obligations raised against the vendor during the evaluation period due to under-delivery against IO commitments. A make-good is compensatory inventory provided by the vendor to offset shortfalls.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.mrc_accreditation_status IS 'Current MRC (Media Rating Council) accreditation status of the vendor at the time of evaluation. MRC accreditation validates the vendor''s measurement methodologies and is required for audience measurement and impression counting credibility.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.overall_scorecard_rating IS 'Composite weighted scorecard rating for the vendor for the evaluation period, typically on a scale of 0.00 to 10.00 or 0.00 to 100.00. Aggregates delivery fulfillment, invoice accuracy, SLA adherence, brand safety, and viewability dimensions into a single performance score used for preferred vendor list tier assignment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.preferred_vendor_tier IS 'Preferred vendor list tier assignment resulting from this evaluation. Tier 1 indicates top-performing strategic partners; Tier 2 indicates approved vendors; Tier 3 indicates conditional approval; Probation indicates performance improvement required; Disqualified indicates removal from preferred vendor list.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.prior_preferred_vendor_tier IS 'The vendor''s preferred vendor list tier from the immediately preceding evaluation period. Used to track tier movement (promotion or demotion) resulting from this evaluation cycle.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.prior_scorecard_rating IS 'The vendor''s overall scorecard rating from the immediately preceding evaluation period. Enables quarter-over-quarter trend analysis and identification of improving or declining vendor performance trajectories.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.response_time_sla_adherence_rate IS 'Percentage of vendor response obligations (e.g., campaign issue resolution, data discrepancy responses, creative trafficking requests) fulfilled within the contractually agreed SLA response time during the evaluation period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.scorecard_rating_scale IS 'The numeric scale used for the overall_scorecard_rating in this evaluation (e.g., 0-10, 0-100, 1-5). Ensures correct interpretation of the rating value across different evaluation frameworks or vendor categories.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.sla_breaches_count IS 'Number of SLA response obligations that were not fulfilled within the contractually agreed timeframe during the evaluation period. Used to identify chronic SLA non-compliance patterns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.sla_incidents_total IS 'Total number of SLA-governed response obligations raised against the vendor during the evaluation period. Denominator for response_time_sla_adherence_rate calculation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.tag_certification_status IS 'Current TAG (Trustworthy Accountability Group) certification status of the vendor at the time of evaluation. TAG certification is a prerequisite for preferred vendor list tier 1 eligibility and indicates compliance with anti-fraud, brand safety, and supply chain transparency standards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.total_invoices_submitted IS 'Total number of invoices submitted by the vendor during the evaluation period. Denominator for invoice accuracy rate calculation. Sourced from Mediaocean Prisma billing records.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.vendor_category IS 'Classification of the vendor type being evaluated. Determines which performance dimensions and benchmarks are applicable. Code set: ref.vendor_category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.vendor_dispute_flag IS 'Indicates whether the vendor has formally disputed the findings of this performance evaluation. When True, the evaluation status should reflect ''disputed'' and a resolution process must be initiated.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.vendor_dispute_notes IS 'Free-text notes capturing the vendor''s formal objection or dispute rationale when vendor_dispute_flag is True. Documents the basis of the dispute for audit trail and resolution tracking purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.viewability_rate IS 'Percentage of impressions delivered by the vendor during the evaluation period that met the MRC (Media Rating Council) viewability standard (50% of pixels in view for 1 continuous second for display; 50% for 2 seconds for video). Key quality metric for media vendor evaluation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.performance_evaluation.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE vendor.reconciliation IS 'Media cost reconciliation record comparing IO-authorized spend against vendor-invoiced amounts and actual delivery data from ad servers (CM360, The Trade Desk). Captures reconciliation period, variance amount, variance percentage, discrepancy reason code, resolution status, and approved final billing amount. Supports Mediaocean Prisma post-buy reconciliation and SAP S/4HANA financial close processes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.reconciliation_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for the media cost reconciliation record. Primary key for this entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Reconciliations track delivered spend by brand for budget management. Multi-brand advertisers reconcile vendor invoices at brand level to ensure accurate brand P&L. Essential for brand-level financial LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the advertising campaign associated with this reconciliation record, enabling campaign-level financial close and post-buy analysis. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: Media reconciliation is performed at the IO level — comparing IO-authorized spend against delivered and invoiced amounts. Linking reconciliation.contract_insertion_order_id enables IO reconciliation r LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: Reconciliations often occur at flight level for multi-flight campaigns to verify delivery and spend. Essential for flight-level discrepancy resolution, makegood tracking, and financial accuracy in adv LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.flight.flight_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Media reconciliations validate vendor billing against project budgets and deliverables. Linking reconciliation to initiative enables project-level financial close, variance reporting, and ensures proj LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.invoice_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.invoice. Business justification: Reconciliation is the process of comparing IO-authorized spend against vendor-invoiced amounts and ad-server-delivered spend. Each reconciliation record analyzes a specific invoice to identify varianc';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.io_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.io_line. Business justification: Reconciliations occur at IO line level to match contracted vs delivered units. Essential for billing disputes, makegood identification, under-delivery penalties, and vendor performance evaluation. Ena';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.line_item_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.line_item. Business justification: Reconciliations commonly reconcile at line-item level for granular delivery verification against contracted units. Critical for line-item-level discrepancy resolution, billing accuracy, and vendor per LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.line_item.line_item_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Reconciliation validates delivered media spend against SOW-level budgets and scope commitments. Finance teams track SOW budget utilization, flag overruns, and trigger SOW amendments when reconciled sp LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.supplier_id IS 'Reference to the third-party media vendor, publisher, or technology partner (DSP/SSP) whose invoice is being reconciled against authorized spend. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.adserver_delivered_amount IS 'Actual media cost derived from ad server delivery data (Google Campaign Manager 360 or The Trade Desk) for the reconciliation period. Used as the authoritative delivery benchmark in post-buy reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.adserver_source IS 'Identifies the authoritative ad serving or DSP platform from which delivery data was sourced for this reconciliation (e.g., Google Campaign Manager 360, The Trade Desk). Ensures traceability of delivery benchmarks.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.approved_billing_amount IS 'The mutually agreed and approved final billing amount after reconciliation resolution. This is the amount posted to SAP S/4HANA for financial close and vendor payment processing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the agency finance or media operations team member who formally approved the final billing amount and closed the reconciliation record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.approved_timestamp IS 'Date and time when the reconciliation record was formally approved and the final billing amount was confirmed. Key lifecycle event for SAP S/4HANA financial period close.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.buying_method IS 'Method by which the media was purchased, distinguishing between direct IO buys, programmatic guaranteed, open RTB (Real-Time Bidding), private marketplace (PMP), or preferred deals. Affects reconciliation workflow and tolerance thresholds.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.channel_type IS 'The media channel category for the spend being reconciled (e.g., Display, Video, CTV/OTT, OOH/DOOH, Search). Enables channel-level reconciliation reporting and variance analysis. Code set: ref.channel_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.credit_note_amount IS 'Monetary value of the vendor-issued credit note applied to resolve an overbilling discrepancy. Reduces the net payable amount in SAP S/4HANA Accounts Payable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.credit_note_number IS 'Vendor-issued credit note reference number when a credit adjustment is issued to resolve an overbilling discrepancy. Linked to SAP S/4HANA Accounts Payable credit memo processing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code applicable to all monetary amounts on this reconciliation record (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR). Supports multi-currency media buying operations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.discrepancy_description IS 'Free-text narrative explaining the specific nature of the billing discrepancy, including details of delivery shortfalls, trafficking errors, or vendor disputes not fully captured by the reason code.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.discrepancy_reason_code IS 'Standardized code classifying the root cause of the billing discrepancy between IO-authorized spend and vendor invoice. Drives resolution workflow and vendor performance tracking. Code set: ref.discrepancy_reason_code.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.due_date IS 'Date by which the approved billing amount must be paid to the vendor per contractual payment terms. Derived from vendor invoice date and agreed net payment terms (e.g., Net 30, Net 60).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.io_authorized_amount IS 'Total media spend amount authorized under the Insertion Order (IO) for the reconciliation period. Represents the contractually committed budget against which vendor invoices are compared.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.makegood_flag IS 'Indicates whether a make-good placement has been agreed as part of the discrepancy resolution, where the vendor compensates for delivery shortfalls with additional inventory rather than a monetary credit.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.notes IS 'Free-text field for additional commentary, escalation notes, or vendor communication summaries relevant to the reconciliation record. Used by media finance teams during dispute resolution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.period_end_date IS 'End date of the media delivery period covered by this reconciliation record. Together with period_start_date defines the reconciliation billing window.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.period_start_date IS 'Start date of the media delivery period covered by this reconciliation record. Defines the billing window for comparing IO-authorized spend against vendor-invoiced amounts.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.prisma_reconciliation_ref IS 'Reference identifier from Mediaocean Prisma post-buy reconciliation module corresponding to this record. Enables traceability between the lakehouse Silver Layer and the source system of record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.reconciliation_number IS 'Externally-known business identifier for this reconciliation record, used in Mediaocean Prisma post-buy workflows and SAP S/4HANA financial close correspondence with vendors.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.reconciliation_status IS 'Current lifecycle state of the reconciliation record within the post-buy financial close workflow. Drives approval routing in Mediaocean Prisma and SAP S/4HANA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.reconciliation_type IS 'Classification of the reconciliation record indicating whether it covers standard media buys, programmatic (RTB/DSP) activity, make-good placements, credit adjustments, or final billing close.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.resolution_date IS 'Date on which the billing discrepancy was formally resolved and the approved billing amount was agreed between the agency and the vendor.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.resolution_status IS 'Current status of the discrepancy resolution process. Tracks whether the variance is unresolved, awaiting vendor response, under internal review, fully resolved, or written off as immaterial.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.sap_document_number IS 'SAP S/4HANA FI accounting document number generated upon financial close posting of the approved billing amount. Provides the audit link between media reconciliation and the general ledger.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.tolerance_threshold_pct IS 'Agreed acceptable variance percentage threshold below which discrepancies are considered immaterial and do not require formal dispute resolution. Typically set per vendor contract or IAB industry standard (commonly 10%).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.variance_amount IS 'Absolute monetary difference between the vendor-invoiced amount and the ad server delivered amount (vendor_invoiced_amount minus adserver_delivered_amount). Positive value indicates vendor overbilling; negative indicates underbilling.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.variance_pct IS 'Variance expressed as a percentage of the IO-authorized amount ((variance_amount / io_authorized_amount) * 100). Used to assess materiality of discrepancy against agency tolerance thresholds (typically ±10% per IAB guidelines).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.vendor_invoiced_amount IS 'Total gross amount billed by the vendor on their invoice for the reconciliation period. Primary input to variance calculation against IO-authorized spend.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.within_tolerance_flag IS 'Indicates whether the variance percentage falls within the agreed tolerance threshold, determining whether formal dispute escalation is required.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN vendor.reconciliation.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE finance.budget_line IS 'Granular line-item breakdown of approved budgets, enabling detailed tracking of spend by campaign flight, media channel, creative production phase, or cost category. Captures parent budget reference, line description, cost category, channel type, flight start/end dates, allocated amount, revised amount, committed amount, actual spend to date, variance amount, variance percentage, and approval status. Feeds margin analysis and P&L reporting at the campaign and account level.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.budget_line_id IS 'Unique identifier for the budget line item. Primary key for the budget line entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Budget lines in media planning are allocated to specific client brands for brand portfolio budget management and spend tracking. budget_line has campaign_id and cost_center_id but no brand reference; LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the campaign this budget line supports. Enables campaign-level budget tracking and reconciliation. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.contract_deliverable_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_deliverable. Business justification: Budget lines fund specific contract deliverables in advertising project accounting. Linking budget_line to contract_deliverable enables deliverable-level cost tracking and actual-vs-estimated cost rep LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_deliverable.contract_deliverable_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: Contract IOs authorize spend that is tracked at the budget line level. Linking budget_line to contract_insertion_order enables spend-vs-commitment reporting — a core financial control in advertising a LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_rate_card. Business justification: Budget lines in advertising are priced against negotiated rate cards. Linking budget_line to contract_rate_card enables rate compliance reporting — finance can verify that committed spend aligns with LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_rate_card.contract_rate_card_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Budget lines are allocated to cost centers for granular expense tracking. Currently references via natural key (cost_center_code). Adding cost_center_id FK enables proper joins and removes redundant c';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.finance_budget_id IS 'Reference to the parent budget that this line item belongs to. Links to the master budget allocation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: Budget lines in advertising are structured around campaign flights. budget_line currently stores flight_start_date and flight_end_date as denormalized plain columns — a flight_id FK normalizes this, e LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.flight.flight_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Budget line items reference GL accounts for detailed cost tracking. Adding gl_account_id FK provides referential integrity. Remove redundant gl_account_code.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.io_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.io_line. Business justification: A finance budget line maps directly to a vendor IO line — the financial authorization corresponds to the contractual commitment. Advertising finance teams use this link to reconcile committed budget a';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.plan_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan_line. Business justification: Budget lines allocated to plan lines for detailed budget management and plan-to-actual variance tracking in media planning. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.plan_line.plan_line_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.supplier_id IS 'Reference to the vendor or supplier associated with this budget line spend. Links to vendor master data for payment processing and reconciliation. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.work_package_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.work_package. Business justification: Budget lines are allocated to specific WBS work packages for granular project cost tracking and WBS-level budget control — standard agency project accounting. Finance teams need to see which work pack LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.work_package.work_package_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.actual_spend IS 'The actual amount spent to date against this budget line, including invoiced and paid expenses. Used for budget variance analysis and burn rate tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.allocated_amount IS 'The original approved budget amount allocated to this line item at the time of budget creation. Represents the baseline budget before any revisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.approval_status IS 'Current approval workflow status of this budget line. Controls whether the line can be committed or spent against.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the person who approved this budget line. Provides audit trail for budget authorization and accountability.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.approved_timestamp IS 'Date and time when this budget line was approved. Critical for audit trail and compliance with financial controls.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.billing_category IS 'Classification of how this budget line will appear on client invoices. Aligns with industry-standard billing practices and client contract terms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.channel_type IS 'The media channel or platform type this budget line is allocated to. Supports channel-level budget analysis and Return on Ad Spend (ROAS) optimization. Code set: ref.channel_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.committed_amount IS 'The amount of budget that has been committed through Insertion Orders (IO), contracts, or purchase orders but not yet invoiced or paid. Represents encumbered funds.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.cost_category IS 'Classification of the budget line by cost type. Determines how the expense is categorized in financial reporting and Profit and Loss (P&L) statements. Code set: ref.cost_category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary amounts in this budget line. Supports multi-currency budget management and consolidation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.is_active IS 'Indicates whether this budget line is currently active and available for spending. Inactive lines are retained for historical reporting but cannot be spent against.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.is_billable IS 'Indicates whether this budget line represents costs that will be billed to the client or absorbed as agency overhead. Critical for margin analysis and client invoicing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.line_description IS 'Detailed textual description of what this budget line covers, including scope, deliverables, and any special conditions or assumptions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.line_number IS 'Sequential line number within the parent budget. Used for ordering and referencing specific line items in budget documentation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.markup_percentage IS 'The percentage markup applied to cost for client billing. Used to calculate gross margin and agency revenue on pass-through costs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.notes IS 'Free-form notes and comments about this budget line. Captures assumptions, constraints, dependencies, or special instructions for budget execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.revised_amount IS 'The current approved budget amount after any revisions, amendments, or reforecasts. Reflects the most up-to-date budget allocation for this line.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.revision_number IS 'Sequential version number tracking how many times this budget line has been revised. Supports change management and audit requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.revision_reason IS 'Textual explanation for why this budget line was revised. Required for financial governance and Quarterly Business Review (QBR) reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.variance_amount IS 'The absolute difference between revised budget amount and actual spend. Positive values indicate under-spend, negative values indicate over-spend.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.variance_percentage IS 'The variance amount expressed as a percentage of the revised budget. Key Performance Indicator (KPI) for budget management and financial control.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.budget_line.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE finance.cost_center IS 'Master record for agency cost centers used to allocate and track expenditures across departments, practice groups, and client accounts. Captures cost center code, name, type (overhead, billable, shared services), owning department, P&L responsibility flag, budget owner, SAP CO cost center reference, active status, and fiscal year applicability. Serves as the foundational organizational unit for management accounting, budget-vs-actual reporting, and overhead allocation in SAP S/4HANA CO module.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.cost_center_id IS 'Unique identifier for the cost center record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.parent_cost_center_id IS 'Reference to the parent cost center in a hierarchical cost center structure. Enables roll-up reporting and multi-level budget consolidation. Null for top-level cost centers.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.allocation_method IS 'The method used to allocate costs from this cost center to other cost objects or client accounts. Direct allocation assigns costs explicitly, activity-based uses cost drivers, headcount allocates by employee count, revenue allocates by revenue contribution, square footage by physical space, and Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) by staffing levels.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.annual_budget_amount IS 'The total approved budget amount allocated to this cost center for the fiscal year. Used for budget-versus-actual variance analysis and financial planning.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.approval_required_flag IS 'Boolean indicator of whether expenditures charged to this cost center require explicit approval before posting. True indicates approval workflow is enforced; false indicates automatic posting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.approval_threshold_amount IS 'The monetary threshold above which expenditures charged to this cost center require additional approval. Amounts below this threshold may be auto-approved based on delegation rules.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.billable_flag IS 'Boolean indicator of whether costs incurred in this cost center are directly billable to clients. True indicates billable work; false indicates non-billable overhead or internal support.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.budget_owner_email IS 'The email address of the budget owner for communication regarding budget approvals, variance reporting, and financial planning.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.budget_owner_name IS 'The name of the individual responsible for managing and approving the budget for this cost center. Typically a department head, practice leader, or senior manager.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.company_code IS 'The company code or legal entity identifier to which this cost center belongs. Used for multi-entity financial consolidation and reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.controlling_area IS 'The controlling area in SAP S/4HANA CO that groups cost centers for management accounting and internal reporting purposes. A controlling area may span multiple company codes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.cost_center_category IS 'High-level functional category of the cost center. Production centers create deliverables, service centers provide internal services, support centers enable operations, sales centers drive revenue, marketing centers manage campaigns, and administration centers handle corporate governance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.cost_center_code IS 'The externally-known unique alphanumeric code identifying the cost center in financial systems and reports. Used as the business identifier in SAP S/4HANA CO module and Mediaocean Prisma billing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.cost_center_name IS 'The human-readable name or title of the cost center, used for display and reporting purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.cost_center_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the cost center. Active centers are operational and accepting charges, inactive centers are temporarily disabled, suspended centers are under review, closed centers are permanently retired, and pending approval centers are awaiting activation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.cost_center_type IS 'Classification of the cost center based on its function and cost allocation model. Overhead centers support general operations, billable centers track client-facing work, shared services centers provide cross-functional support, direct centers relate to revenue-generating activities, indirect centers support operations, and administrative centers manage corporate functions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.cost_pool_flag IS 'Boolean indicator of whether this cost center functions as a cost pool that aggregates costs for subsequent allocation to other cost centers or client accounts. True indicates a cost pool; false indicates a standard cost center.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.currency_code IS 'The three-letter ISO 4217 currency code in which this cost center''s budget and expenses are denominated. Examples include USD, EUR, GBP, CAD.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.effective_end_date IS 'The date on which this cost center configuration ceases to be effective. Null for currently active configurations. Used for historical analysis and audit trails.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.effective_start_date IS 'The date on which this cost center configuration becomes effective and begins accepting cost allocations. Supports temporal validity and historical tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.fiscal_year IS 'The fiscal year for which this cost center configuration is applicable. Cost centers may have different configurations across fiscal years for budget planning and reporting purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.location_code IS 'Three-letter code identifying the primary geographic location or office where this cost center operates. Examples include NYC, LON, SFO, TOR. Used for location-based cost analysis and reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.notes IS 'Free-text field for additional comments, special instructions, or contextual information about the cost center. Used for documentation and knowledge transfer.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.overhead_allocation_percentage IS 'The percentage of overhead costs allocated to this cost center from shared services or administrative cost pools. Used in fully-loaded cost calculations and margin analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.owning_department IS 'The department or organizational unit that owns and manages this cost center. Examples include Creative Services, Media Planning, Account Management, Finance, Human Resources, IT, Operations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.practice_group IS 'The specialized practice area or service line associated with this cost center, such as Digital Marketing, Brand Strategy, Public Relations, Data Analytics, Creative Production, Media Buying.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.profit_and_loss_responsibility_flag IS 'Boolean indicator of whether this cost center has direct profit and loss accountability. True indicates the center is a profit center with revenue and expense responsibility; false indicates a pure cost center.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.quarterly_budget_amount IS 'The budget amount allocated to this cost center for the current quarter. Supports quarterly business review (QBR) processes and short-term financial management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.sap_co_cost_center_reference IS 'The corresponding cost center identifier in the SAP S/4HANA Controlling (CO) module. Used for integration and reconciliation between the lakehouse and the source ERP system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.cost_center.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE finance.finance_budget IS 'Approved financial budget records for campaigns, accounts, cost centers, and agency operations, serving as the control baseline for spend authorization and variance analysis. Captures budget version (original, revised, final), budget type (campaign, overhead, media, production, talent), fiscal year, fiscal period, approved amount, currency, budget owner, approval status, approval date, lock status, SAP CO internal order reference, and Mediaocean Prisma budget reference. Supports budget-vs-actual reporting, EBITDA tracking, and financial governance processes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.finance_budget_id IS 'Unique identifier for the budget record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.agreement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.agreement. Business justification: Master agreements (retainers, MSAs) in advertising have budgets allocated at the agreement level, not just SOW level. Finance teams need to link budgets directly to agreements for annual budget planni LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.agreement.agreement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the campaign this budget is allocated to, if applicable. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.client_brief_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.client_brief. Business justification: Client briefs define campaign objectives, budgets, and deliverables that directly drive budget creation and allocation in advertising operations. Budget planning starts with approved client briefs spe LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.client_brief.client_brief_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.cost_center_id IS 'Reference to the cost center this budget is allocated to for internal financial tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Budget references GL account via natural key (gl_account_code). Adding surrogate key FK gl_account_id enables proper referential integrity. Remove redundant gl_account_code as it can be retrieved via';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Finance budgets in advertising agencies are created to fund specific project initiatives. Finance teams need to link budget records to the initiative for project cost tracking, billing, and budget uti LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: SOWs define the scope and budget for client engagements; finance creates budgets based on SOW commitments for spend control and forecasting. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.allocated_amount IS 'Amount of the budget that has been allocated or committed to specific activities or sub-budgets, but not yet spent.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.approval_date IS 'Date when the budget was officially approved by the authorized approver.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.approval_status IS 'Current approval workflow status of the budget: draft (being prepared), pending (awaiting approval), approved (authorized for use), rejected (not approved), cancelled (voided).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.approved_amount IS 'The total approved budget amount in the specified currency. This is the baseline for spend authorization and variance analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the individual who approved the budget.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.budget_category IS 'High-level financial category of the budget: operating (day-to-day operational expenses), capital (long-term asset investments), project (specific project-based allocation), discretionary (flexible spend allocation).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.budget_description IS 'Detailed description of the budget purpose, scope, and any special conditions or notes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.budget_name IS 'Descriptive name of the budget for easy identification and reporting purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.budget_number IS 'Externally-known unique business identifier for the budget record, used for reference in financial documents and approvals.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.budget_type IS 'Classification of the budget by its purpose: campaign (client campaign spend), overhead (agency operational costs), media (media buying allocation), production (creative production costs), talent (talent and usage rights fees), creative (creative development costs).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the approved budget amount (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.effective_end_date IS 'Date when this budget expires and spend authorization ends. Nullable for open-ended budgets.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.effective_start_date IS 'Date when this budget becomes effective and spend authorization begins.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.fiscal_period IS 'The fiscal period (month or quarter) within the fiscal year this budget applies to, typically 1-12 for monthly periods or 1-4 for quarterly periods.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.fiscal_year IS 'The fiscal year this budget applies to, represented as a four-digit year (e.g., 2024).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.lock_status IS 'Indicates whether the budget is locked (true) and cannot be modified, or unlocked (false) and can still be edited. Locked budgets are typically final versions used for variance reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.mediaocean_prisma_budget_reference IS 'Reference identifier to the corresponding budget record in Mediaocean Prisma for media planning and billing reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.owner IS 'Name or identifier of the individual or role responsible for managing and authorizing spend against this budget.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.profit_center_code IS 'Profit center code in SAP S/4HANA CO for Profit and Loss (P&L) reporting and margin analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.remaining_amount IS 'Remaining unspent budget amount, calculated as approved amount minus spent amount and allocated amount.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.revision_number IS 'Sequential revision number tracking how many times this budget has been revised. Original budget is revision 0.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.revision_reason IS 'Business justification or reason for the most recent budget revision.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.sap_co_internal_order IS 'Reference to the SAP S/4HANA CO internal order number used for cost collection and budget control in the ERP system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.spent_amount IS 'Actual amount spent against this budget to date, used for budget-vs-actual variance analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.variance_threshold_percent IS 'Acceptable variance threshold as a percentage of the approved budget. Exceeding this threshold triggers alerts or requires additional approval.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.version IS 'Version status of the budget: original (initial approved budget), revised (updated after changes), final (locked final version), forecast (projected budget for planning).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.finance_budget.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE finance.gl_account IS 'General ledger chart of accounts master for the agency, aligned to SAP S/4HANA FI module. Captures account code, account name, account type (asset, liability, equity, revenue, expense), financial statement category, P&L vs balance sheet classification, cost element linkage, currency, consolidation group, IFRS/GAAP mapping, and active status. Serves as the SSOT for all ledger account definitions used in journal entries, billing, and financial reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.gl_account_id IS 'Unique identifier for the general ledger account. Primary key for the GL account master data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.account_code IS 'The externally-known unique account number used in financial transactions and reporting. Typically a 4-10 digit numeric code aligned to the chart of accounts structure.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.account_description_long IS 'Extended description or explanatory text for the general ledger account, providing additional context, usage guidelines, or business rules for posting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.account_group IS 'The hierarchical grouping or category within the chart of accounts (e.g., ''Current Assets'', ''Operating Expenses'', ''Client Revenue''). Used for rollup and reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.account_name IS 'The human-readable name or title of the general ledger account (e.g., ''Media Costs - Digital'', ''Client Revenue - Retainer'', ''Salaries and Wages'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.account_type IS 'The fundamental accounting classification of the account: asset, liability, equity, revenue, or expense. Determines the account''s role in the balance sheet or profit and loss statement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.balance_sheet_classification IS 'The detailed balance sheet classification for asset, liability, and equity accounts: current asset, non-current asset, current liability, non-current liability, equity, or not applicable (for P&L accounts).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.chart_of_accounts IS 'The chart of accounts identifier to which this account belongs. Defines the account structure and numbering scheme for the organization or group.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.company_code IS 'The SAP company code (legal entity identifier) to which this account belongs. Supports multi-entity chart of accounts with company-specific configurations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.consolidation_group IS 'The consolidation grouping code used for corporate group financial consolidation and elimination entries. Aligns accounts across legal entities for consolidated reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.cost_center_applicable IS 'Indicates whether this account requires cost center assignment for expense tracking and allocation. True if cost center is mandatory for postings to this account.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.cost_element IS 'The cost element code linking this GL account to the controlling (CO) module for cost center and internal order tracking. Used for management accounting and margin analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.currency_code IS 'The three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the account''s local currency (e.g., ''USD'', ''EUR'', ''GBP''). Determines the currency in which balances are maintained.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.field_status_group IS 'The field status group code that controls which fields are required, optional, or hidden when posting to this account. Enforces data entry rules at the account level.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.financial_statement_category IS 'The primary financial statement to which this account belongs: balance sheet, income statement (P&L), cash flow statement, or statement of equity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.gaap_mapping IS 'The US GAAP account classification or line item code to which this account maps for GAAP-compliant financial reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.gl_account_status IS 'The current lifecycle status of the general ledger account: active (in use), inactive (not in use but retained), pending (awaiting approval), or archived (historical only).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.ifrs_mapping IS 'The IFRS account classification or line item code to which this account maps for IFRS-compliant financial reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.line_item_display IS 'Indicates whether individual line items (journal entry details) are stored and displayed for this account. True if line-item reporting is enabled; false if only totals are maintained.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.open_item_management IS 'Indicates whether this account uses open item management for tracking and clearing individual postings (e.g., invoices, payments). True if open item clearing is required.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.pl_classification IS 'The detailed profit and loss classification for revenue and expense accounts: operating revenue, non-operating revenue, cost of sales, operating expense, non-operating expense, or not applicable (for balance sheet accounts).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.posting_blocked IS 'Indicates whether direct postings to this account are currently blocked. True if the account is locked for new transactions (e.g., during period close or account deactivation).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.profit_center_applicable IS 'Indicates whether this account requires profit center assignment for P&L segmentation and profitability analysis. True if profit center is mandatory for postings to this account.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.reconciliation_account IS 'Indicates whether this is a reconciliation account (control account) that summarizes subledger balances (e.g., accounts receivable, accounts payable, vendor accounts). True if this account is managed by a subledger.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.sort_key IS 'The sort key or allocation field used for automatic assignment of posting keys, document numbers, or payment terms during transaction entry.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.tax_category IS 'The tax category or tax code applicable to this account for automatic tax calculation and reporting (e.g., ''VAT Standard'', ''Sales Tax Exempt'', ''Input Tax'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.valid_from_date IS 'The date from which this general ledger account is valid and available for use in financial transactions. Supports time-dependent account structures.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.valid_to_date IS 'The date until which this general ledger account is valid. Null if the account is open-ended. Used for account retirement and historical tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.gl_account.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE finance.client_invoice IS 'Authoritative record of invoices issued by the agency to advertising clients for services rendered, media placements, and production work. Captures invoice number, invoice date, due date, billing period, client account reference, SOW/IO reference, invoice type (retainer, project, media, production), line item summary, subtotal, tax amount, total amount, currency, payment terms (net 30/60/90), payment status, SAP FI document number, and Mediaocean Prisma billing reference. Core to revenue recognition and accounts receivable management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.client_invoice_id IS 'Unique identifier for the client invoice record. Primary key for the client invoice entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the client advertiser account being invoiced. Links invoice to the client master record. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.agency_relationship_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.agency_relationship. Business justification: Invoices are issued under specific AOR or project-based agency-client agreements. Linking invoices to agency_relationship supports commission rate application, relationship-level billing reconciliatio LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.agency_relationship.agency_relationship_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Client invoices in advertising are issued at the brand level (brand-specific campaigns and services). Brand-level accounts receivable aging and invoice reporting are standard agency finance operations LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.buy_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.buy. Business justification: Client invoices for media services reference specific buys for billing substantiation. Buy-level invoice tracking enables agencies to provide clients with detailed billing support and supports billing LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.buy.buy_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.campaign_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.campaign. Business justification: Client invoices in advertising are issued per campaign. A campaign_id FK on client_invoice enables campaign-level billing reconciliation, revenue attribution reporting, and dispute resolution — a name LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: IOs are invoiced to clients; finance links invoices back to the authorizing IO for reconciliation and payment tracking. Replaces denormalized io_reference_number. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Client invoices are attributed to cost centers for revenue tracking and P&L allocation. Adding cost_center_id FK replaces natural key reference (cost_center_code).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.delivery_pacing_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.delivery_pacing. Business justification: Client invoices are validated against delivery pacing records to confirm billed amounts reflect actual delivery. Finance teams use pacing data to support invoice accuracy, dispute resolution, and clie LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.delivery_pacing.delivery_pacing_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.milestone_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.milestone. Business justification: Agency client invoices are frequently triggered by project milestone completion (campaign launch, creative delivery gates). project_milestone has is_billing_trigger flag confirming this pattern. Billi LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.milestone.milestone_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.performance_kpi_target_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.performance_kpi_target. Business justification: Performance-based invoicing validates delivery against contractual KPI targets; billing adjustments require linking to target definitions. LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.performance_kpi_target.performance_kpi_target_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.plan_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan. Business justification: Client invoices for media services reference the media plan for billing reconciliation and client reporting. Agencies invoice clients against approved media plans; this link enables plan-level billing LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.plan.plan_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: SOWs are the contractual basis for client invoicing; invoice lines reference SOW terms and deliverables. Replaces denormalized sow_reference_number with proper FK. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.adjustment_amount IS 'Additional adjustments applied to the invoice (credits, surcharges, reconciliation adjustments). Can be positive or negative.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.amount_outstanding IS 'Remaining unpaid balance on the invoice. Calculated as total_amount minus amount_paid. Zero when invoice is fully paid.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.amount_paid IS 'Total amount received from the client against this invoice. Used to track partial payments and calculate outstanding balance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the agency employee who approved the invoice for issuance. Used for internal approval audit trail.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.approved_timestamp IS 'Date and time when the invoice was approved for issuance. Marks transition from draft to issued status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.billing_contact_email IS 'Email address of the billing contact for invoice delivery and payment correspondence. Primary communication channel for accounts receivable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.billing_contact_name IS 'Name of the client contact responsible for invoice receipt and payment processing. Used for invoice delivery and payment follow-up.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.billing_period_end_date IS 'End date of the period covered by this invoice. Defines the scope of services or media placements included in the billing cycle.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.billing_period_start_date IS 'Start date of the period covered by this invoice. Relevant for retainer billing, subscription services, and time-based billing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the invoice (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP). Defines the monetary unit for all amounts.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.discount_amount IS 'Total discount applied to the invoice. May include volume discounts, early payment discounts, or negotiated rate reductions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.dispute_date IS 'Date when the client raised a dispute on this invoice. Used for dispute aging and resolution tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.dispute_reason IS 'Reason provided by client for disputing the invoice. Populated when invoice_status is disputed. Used for dispute resolution tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.due_date IS 'Date by which payment is expected from the client based on agreed payment terms. Used for accounts receivable aging and collections management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.invoice_date IS 'Date the invoice was issued to the client. Used for revenue recognition timing and aging analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.invoice_notes IS 'Free-text notes or special instructions related to the invoice. May include payment instructions, billing clarifications, or client-specific requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.invoice_number IS 'Externally-visible unique invoice number issued to the client. Used for client communication, payment reference, and accounts receivable tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.invoice_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the invoice: draft (not yet finalized), issued (approved for sending), sent (delivered to client), partially_paid (payment in progress), paid (fully settled), overdue (past due date), disputed (under client review), cancelled (voided). Code set: ref.invoice_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.invoice_type IS 'Classification of the invoice based on billing model: retainer (recurring fee), project (fixed scope), media (placement costs), production (creative development), pass_through (third-party costs), or adjustment (credit/debit memo).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.mediaocean_billing_reference IS 'Reference identifier from Mediaocean Prisma billing system for media cost reconciliation and invoice generation. Links to media buy billing records.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.payment_method IS 'Expected or preferred payment method for this invoice: wire transfer, ACH (Automated Clearing House), check, credit card, or direct debit.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.payment_received_date IS 'Date when full or final payment was received from the client. Null if invoice is unpaid or partially paid.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.payment_terms IS 'Agreed payment terms defining when payment is due: net_15 (15 days), net_30 (30 days), net_45 (45 days), net_60 (60 days), net_90 (90 days), due_on_receipt (immediate), custom (non-standard terms). Code set: ref.payment_terms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.purchase_order_number IS 'Client purchase order number required for invoice processing. Many clients require PO reference for accounts payable approval.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.revenue_recognition_date IS 'Date when revenue from this invoice is recognized in financial statements. May differ from invoice date based on revenue recognition rules.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.sap_fi_document_number IS 'SAP S/4HANA FI document number for the accounting entry created from this invoice. Links invoice to general ledger posting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.sent_timestamp IS 'Date and time when the invoice was sent to the client. Used for tracking invoice delivery and aging calculations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.subtotal_amount IS 'Total invoice amount before taxes, discounts, or adjustments. Sum of all line item charges.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.tax_amount IS 'Total tax amount applied to the invoice (sales tax, VAT, GST). Calculated based on jurisdiction and tax rules.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.total_amount IS 'Final total amount due from the client. Calculated as subtotal + tax - discount + adjustment. This is the amount the client must pay.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.client_invoice.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE finance.invoice_line IS 'Individual line items on a client invoice, capturing the detailed breakdown of billable services, media costs, production fees, and agency commissions. Captures invoice reference, line number, service description, billing code, quantity, unit rate, line amount, tax code, revenue recognition category, campaign reference, cost center, GL account code, and delivery confirmation flag. Enables granular revenue recognition and client billing transparency per IAB billing standards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.invoice_line_id IS 'Unique identifier for the invoice line item. Primary key for the invoice_line product.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.budget_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.budget_line. Business justification: Each invoice line item should be traceable to the specific budget line it is billing against. invoice_line already has revenue_recognition_category and revenue_recognition_date, indicating it is a fin';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.buy_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.buy. Business justification: Invoice lines bill specific media buys for detailed cost recovery and margin calculation - essential billing granularity. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.buy.buy_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the advertising campaign associated with this billable line item. Links revenue to campaign performance. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.click_event_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.click_event. Business justification: Invoice lines for CPC campaigns bill specific click volumes; delivery confirmation requires linking to click events. LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.click_event.click_event_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.client_invoice_id IS 'Reference to the parent invoice header. Links this line item to the overall client invoice.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Invoice line items are allocated to cost centers for detailed revenue attribution. Currently has cost_center (STRING) natural key. Adding cost_center_id FK provides referential integrity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.creative_deliverable_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.creative_deliverable. Business justification: Invoice lines bill clients for specific creative deliverables. Links billing to deliverables for revenue attribution, deliverable-level profitability analysis, and reconciliation of billed vs. deliver LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.creative_deliverable.creative_deliverable_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.deliverable_tracker_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.deliverable_tracker. Business justification: Invoice lines in advertising are billed for specific project deliverables (TV spots, banner sets, reports). Linking invoice_line to deliverable_tracker enables billing reconciliation against project d LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.deliverable_tracker.deliverable_tracker_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.delivery_pacing_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.delivery_pacing. Business justification: Invoice lines are reconciled against delivery pacing at placement/line-item level to validate billed quantities. This line-level delivery validation is essential for accurate CPM/CPC billing and suppo LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.delivery_pacing.delivery_pacing_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Invoice line items post to GL revenue accounts. Adding gl_account_id FK replaces natural key reference (gl_account_code).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.io_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.io_line. Business justification: Client invoice lines in advertising are derived from vendor IO line delivery data. This link supports billing reconciliation and agency margin analysis by tracing each billed line back to the specific';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_insertion_order. Business justification: Invoice lines reference insertion orders for billing detail, reconciliation, and revenue allocation - core billing granularity in advertising finance. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_insertion_order.media_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.media_placement_id IS 'Reference to the specific media placement being billed. Links invoice line to media execution details. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_placement.media_placement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.performance_kpi_target_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.performance_kpi_target. Business justification: Invoice lines for performance-based billing reference specific KPI targets (guaranteed viewability, CPA rates). Linking invoice_line to performance_kpi_target supports performance-based billing valida LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.performance_kpi_target.performance_kpi_target_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.plan_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan_line. Business justification: Invoice lines reference plan lines for billing against planned spend and budget variance tracking in client billing processes. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.plan_line.plan_line_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.programmatic_deal_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.programmatic_deal. Business justification: Programmatic deal invoice lines must reference the originating deal for billing reconciliation and DSP platform cost verification. Deal-level invoice line tracking is required for programmatic spend a LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.programmatic_deal.programmatic_deal_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.reconciliation_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.reconciliation. Business justification: Client invoice lines are generated after vendor reconciliation confirms delivery. Linking invoice_line to the reconciliation record that validated delivery is standard advertising billing practice, en';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.revenue_recognition_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.revenue_recognition. Business justification: invoice_line already carries revenue_recognition_category and revenue_recognition_date attributes, indicating that revenue recognition is determined at the line level (different service lines may use';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.schedule_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.schedule. Business justification: Broadcast invoice lines reference specific schedule entries for billing verification against aired spots. Affidavit reconciliation in broadcast billing requires matching invoice lines to schedule reco LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.schedule.schedule_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.viewability_measurement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.viewability_measurement. Business justification: Invoice lines for viewability-guaranteed placements bill based on viewable impressions; requires linking to viewability measurement data. LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.viewability_measurement.viewability_measurement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.billing_code IS 'Internal billing classification code used to categorize the type of service or cost being invoiced. Maps to agency billing taxonomy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.billing_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of this invoice line item. Tracks progression through billing workflow from draft to final billing. Code set: ref.billing_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.commission_amount IS 'Total agency commission earned on this line item. Represents agency revenue on media pass-through costs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.commission_percentage IS 'Agency commission rate applied to media costs. Standard agency markup percentage per client contract terms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the line amount. Supports multi-currency billing for global clients.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.delivery_confirmation_date IS 'Date on which service delivery was confirmed by client or operations. Triggers revenue recognition eligibility.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.delivery_confirmed_flag IS 'Indicates whether service delivery has been confirmed and validated. True when performance obligation is fulfilled and documented.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.discount_amount IS 'Absolute monetary discount applied to this line item. Reduces the line amount before tax calculation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.discount_percentage IS 'Percentage discount applied to this line item. Reflects negotiated client discounts, volume rebates, or promotional adjustments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.dispute_flag IS 'Indicates whether this line item is under client dispute. True when client has challenged the charge and resolution is pending.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.dispute_reason IS 'Client-provided reason for disputing this invoice line item. Documents the nature of the billing disagreement for resolution tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.line_amount IS 'Total monetary value for this invoice line before tax. Calculated as quantity multiplied by unit rate, adjusted for discounts or markups.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.line_number IS 'Sequential line number within the invoice. Determines the ordering and presentation sequence of line items on the invoice document.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.line_total IS 'Total amount for this invoice line including tax. Sum of line amount and tax amount, representing the final billable value.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.notes IS 'Free-form notes and comments related to this invoice line item. Captures billing instructions, special terms, or clarifications.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.purchase_order_number IS 'Client purchase order number authorizing this expenditure. Required for client accounts payable processing and payment matching.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.quantity IS 'Numeric quantity of units being billed. Represents impressions, hours, days, or other unit of measure depending on service type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.revenue_recognition_category IS 'Classification of revenue recognition status for this line item. Determines timing of revenue realization per accounting standards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.revenue_recognition_date IS 'Date on which revenue for this line item is recognized in the general ledger. Drives financial period allocation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.service_category IS 'High-level categorization of the billable service. Enables revenue analysis by service type and supports P&L reporting by business line. Code set: ref.service_category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.service_description IS 'Detailed narrative description of the billable service, media cost, production fee, or agency commission. Appears on the client-facing invoice document.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.service_end_date IS 'End date of the service period being billed. Defines the completion of the performance obligation delivery window.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.service_start_date IS 'Start date of the service period being billed. Defines the beginning of the performance obligation delivery window.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.tax_amount IS 'Total tax amount applied to this invoice line. Calculated based on tax code and applicable jurisdiction rates.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.tax_code IS 'Tax classification code determining the applicable tax treatment for this line item. Maps to tax jurisdiction and rate tables.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.unit_of_measure IS 'The unit by which quantity is measured. Defines how the billable service is quantified for pricing purposes. Code set: ref.unit_of_measure.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.unit_rate IS 'Price per unit of measure. The rate applied to quantity to calculate the line amount before adjustments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.invoice_line.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE finance.media_cost_reconciliation IS 'Reconciliation records matching planned media costs (from IOs and media plans) against actual vendor invoices and third-party delivery confirmations from Mediaocean Prisma, Google Campaign Manager 360, and DSP platforms. Captures media buy reference, IO number, planned cost, billed cost, delivered impressions, reconciled amount, variance amount, variance reason (under-delivery, rate discrepancy, make-good), reconciliation status (open, in-dispute, cleared), billing period, vendor reference, and Mediaocean Prisma reconciliation document number. Core to sequential liability management and client billing integrity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.media_cost_reconciliation_id IS 'Unique identifier for the media cost reconciliation record. Primary key for this entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.budget_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.budget_line. Business justification: Media cost reconciliation matches planned media costs against actual vendor costs. The budget_line is the planning instrument that defines the planned_cost_amount, channel_type, and flight dates for a';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.buy_id IS 'Reference to the media buy that this reconciliation record pertains to. Links to the media buy master record. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.buy.buy_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.campaign_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.campaign. Business justification: Media cost reconciliation is executed at the campaign level — comparing planned vs. billed media costs per campaign is a core advertising finance process. Enables campaign-level reconciliation reports LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.click_event_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.click_event. Business justification: Click discrepancy reconciliation between ad server and publisher systems; financial adjustments require linking to click events. LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.click_event.click_event_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.conversion_event_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.conversion_event. Business justification: CPA/CPC media buys require reconciliation of billed costs against conversion events. Finance teams validate vendor invoices by matching billed conversion counts to actual conversion event records duri LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.conversion_event.conversion_event_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.cost_center_id IS 'FK to finance.cost_center';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.delivery_pacing_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.delivery_pacing. Business justification: Pacing data informs reconciliation of planned vs actual delivery and spend; variance analysis requires pacing metrics. LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.delivery_pacing.delivery_pacing_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: Billing periods in advertising align with campaign flights. Reconciling media costs at the flight level (planned impressions/spend per flight vs. vendor invoice) is standard practice. Enables flight-l LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.flight.flight_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.io_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.io_line. Business justification: Media cost reconciliation in advertising is performed at the IO line level — each contracted line has its own planned units and spend. Linking reconciliation to the specific IO line enables line-level';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.line_item_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.line_item. Business justification: Line-item-level media cost reconciliation is standard in programmatic and direct advertising — each line item has booked impressions/cost that must be reconciled against vendor delivery. Enables granu LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.line_item.line_item_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_insertion_order. Business justification: Reconciliation is performed at the IO level in agency billing operations. The existing io_number plain attribute is a denormalized reference; a proper FK replaces it. IO-level reconciliation is requir LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_insertion_order.media_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.media_placement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_placement. Business justification: Media cost reconciliation matches billed costs against contracted placement values. Linking reconciliation records to specific placements enables placement-level billing dispute resolution and varianc LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_placement.media_placement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.performance_kpi_target_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.performance_kpi_target. Business justification: Media cost reconciliation validates actual delivery against contracted KPI targets (guaranteed CPM, viewability thresholds). Linking to performance_kpi_target supports contractual delivery validation LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.performance_kpi_target.performance_kpi_target_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.plan_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan_line. Business justification: Reconciliation against plan lines enables planned-vs-actual spend variance reporting at the line level — a standard agency financial control process. Finance teams require this link to produce budget LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.plan_line.plan_line_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.reconciliation_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.reconciliation. Business justification: Finance-side media cost reconciliation must be matched to the vendor-side reconciliation record to close the billing cycle. Advertising operations teams use this cross-domain match to confirm both par';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.supplier_id IS 'Identifier for the media vendor or publisher who provided the media inventory and submitted the invoice. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.vendor_invoice_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.invoice. Business justification: Media cost reconciliation is always performed against a specific vendor invoice — comparing billed amounts to planned costs. This is the foundational link for advertising media billing reconciliation';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.vendor_payable_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.vendor_payable. Business justification: Media cost reconciliations match planned media costs against actual vendor invoices and result in vendor payables being created or adjusted. This FK links the reconciliation to the resulting vendor pa';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.video_completion_event_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.video_completion_event. Business justification: CPCV video buys are reconciled by matching billed completion counts to actual video completion events. This reconciliation step is mandatory for validating vendor invoices on completion-based video ca LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.video_completion_event.video_completion_event_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.viewability_measurement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.viewability_measurement. Business justification: Viewability discrepancies drive make-goods and financial adjustments; reconciliation requires linking to viewability measurement data. LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.viewability_measurement.viewability_measurement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.actual_cpm IS 'The actual cost per thousand impressions calculated from billed cost and delivered impressions. Calculated as (billed_cost_amount / delivered_impressions) * 1000.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the person who approved the final reconciled amount. Used for accountability and audit trail.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.approved_timestamp IS 'Date and time when the reconciliation was formally approved for payment processing and client billing. Represents the completion of the reconciliation workflow.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.billed_cost_amount IS 'The actual cost amount invoiced by the vendor for the media delivery. Represents the vendor''s claim for payment based on delivered impressions or placements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.billing_period_end_date IS 'End date of the billing period covered by this reconciliation record. Defines the conclusion of the media delivery window being reconciled.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.billing_period_start_date IS 'Start date of the billing period covered by this reconciliation record. Defines the beginning of the media delivery window being reconciled.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.cpm_variance IS 'The difference between planned CPM and actual CPM. Used to identify rate discrepancies and pricing issues.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary amounts in this reconciliation record. Ensures consistent currency handling across multi-currency campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.delivered_impressions IS 'The actual number of impressions delivered by the vendor as confirmed by third-party ad serving platforms (Google Campaign Manager 360, DSP platforms). Used for delivery variance calculation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.dispute_flag IS 'Boolean indicator of whether this reconciliation record is currently under dispute. True indicates active dispute; False indicates no dispute or resolved dispute.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.dispute_opened_date IS 'Date when a dispute was formally opened for this reconciliation record. Null if no dispute has been raised.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.dispute_resolution_notes IS 'Free-text notes documenting the dispute resolution process, including vendor communications, adjustments made, and final agreement terms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.dispute_resolved_date IS 'Date when the dispute was formally resolved and the reconciliation was cleared. Null if dispute is still open or no dispute was raised.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.gl_posting_date IS 'Date when the reconciled amount was posted to the general ledger in SAP S/4HANA FI. Used for financial period closing and P&L reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.impression_variance IS 'The difference between planned impressions and delivered impressions. Positive values indicate over-delivery; negative values indicate under-delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.impression_variance_percentage IS 'The impression variance expressed as a percentage of planned impressions. Calculated as (impression_variance / planned_impressions) * 100. Used for delivery performance tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.make_good_flag IS 'Boolean indicator of whether this reconciliation includes make-good impressions provided by the vendor to compensate for under-delivery or quality issues.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.make_good_impressions IS 'Number of additional impressions provided by the vendor as make-good compensation. Null or zero if no make-good was provided.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.payment_due_date IS 'Date by which payment to the vendor is due based on contract payment terms. Used for accounts payable scheduling and cash flow management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.planned_cost_amount IS 'The originally planned media cost as specified in the insertion order and media plan. Represents the budgeted amount for this media buy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.planned_cpm IS 'The planned cost per thousand impressions as negotiated in the media buy. Used as the baseline rate for cost reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.planned_impressions IS 'The number of impressions originally planned and contracted in the insertion order. Used as the baseline for delivery reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.reconciled_amount IS 'The final agreed-upon cost amount after reconciliation adjustments, dispute resolution, and variance analysis. This is the amount approved for payment and client billing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.reconciliation_document_number IS 'Unique document number generated by Mediaocean Prisma for this reconciliation transaction. Used for audit trail and cross-system reference.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.reconciliation_status IS 'Current workflow status of the reconciliation record. Tracks the lifecycle from initial variance detection through dispute resolution to final clearance and payment approval.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.third_party_verification_date IS 'Date when the third-party verification data was received or confirmed. Used for audit trail and data freshness tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.third_party_verification_source IS 'Name of the third-party ad serving or verification platform that provided the delivered impressions data (e.g., Google Campaign Manager 360, The Trade Desk, Nielsen, Comscore).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.variance_amount IS 'The difference between planned cost and reconciled amount. Positive values indicate over-billing or over-delivery; negative values indicate under-delivery or cost savings.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.variance_percentage IS 'The variance amount expressed as a percentage of the planned cost. Calculated as (variance_amount / planned_cost_amount) * 100. Used for threshold-based alerting and variance reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.variance_reason_code IS 'Standardized code indicating the primary reason for the cost variance. Used for root cause analysis and vendor performance tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.variance_reason_description IS 'Detailed free-text explanation of the variance reason, including context, supporting evidence, and resolution notes. Provides audit trail for financial reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.vendor_reference IS 'External reference identifier provided by the media vendor or publisher for this billing cycle. May include invoice number or billing statement reference.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.media_cost_reconciliation.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE finance.payment IS 'Records of actual cash payments made to vendors (AP disbursements) and received from clients (AR receipts), serving as the SSOT for all cash movement events. Captures payment reference number, payment date, payment direction (inbound/outbound), payment method (ACH, wire, check, credit card), payer/payee reference, linked invoice or payable reference, payment amount, currency, exchange rate applied, bank account reference, clearing document number, SAP FI payment document number, reconciliation status, and value date. Supports cash flow forecasting, bank reconciliation, DSO/DPO calculation, and working capital management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.payment_id IS 'Unique identifier for the payment transaction record. Primary key for the payment entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the client or advertiser associated with this payment. Populated for inbound AR receipts and client-related outbound payments. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.buy_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.buy. Business justification: Vendor payments are made against specific media buys in agency operations. Direct buy-to-payment linkage enables buy-level payment status tracking and cash flow reporting. Agency finance teams require LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.buy.buy_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.client_invoice_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.client_invoice. Business justification: Payments can be AR receipts from clients applied to client invoices. The existing invoice_id FK points to vendor.invoice for AP disbursements; this new FK handles client payment receipts. Enables trac';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.invoice_id IS 'Reference to the invoice being settled by this payment. Links payment to the originating billing document for reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_insertion_order. Business justification: Payments allocated to insertion orders for cash flow tracking and payment reconciliation in media finance operations. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_insertion_order.media_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.original_payment_id IS 'Reference to the original payment record that this payment reverses. Populated only when is_reversal is True.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.reconciliation_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.reconciliation. Business justification: Advertising agency payments to vendors are authorized by an approved reconciliation record. Linking payment to the reconciliation that triggered it supports the payment release audit trail and is requ';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.supplier_id IS 'Reference to the vendor, publisher, or supplier associated with this payment. Populated for outbound AP disbursements. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.vendor_payable_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.vendor_payable. Business justification: Payments to vendors settle vendor payables (AP liabilities). This FK links the payment to the vendor payable record it is settling, enabling AP aging and payment application tracking. The existing inv';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.amount IS 'The gross monetary value of the payment transaction in the specified currency. Represents the total cash movement before any adjustments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.approval_date IS 'The date on which the payment was approved. Null if not yet approved or if approval is not required.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.approval_status IS 'Indicates whether the payment has been approved for processing: pending approval (awaiting authorization), approved (authorized for execution), or rejected (denied by approver).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.approved_by IS 'The name or identifier of the person who approved the payment for processing. Used for audit trail and segregation of duties compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.bank_transaction_reference IS 'The unique transaction identifier assigned by the bank or payment processor. Used for bank reconciliation and dispute resolution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.channel IS 'The interface or channel through which the payment was initiated or received: online portal, mobile app, direct bank transfer, lockbox service, manual entry by AP/AR clerk, or API integration.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.clearing_document_number IS 'The document number assigned during the clearing process in the financial system. Links payment to the clearing entry that offsets the receivable or payable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code representing the currency in which the payment was made (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP, JPY).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.direction IS 'Indicates whether this is a payment received from a client (inbound/AR receipt) or a payment made to a vendor (outbound/AP disbursement).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.discount_amount IS 'The monetary value of any early payment discount or settlement discount applied to this payment. Null if no discount was taken.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.exchange_rate IS 'The foreign exchange rate applied to convert the payment amount to the agency''s functional currency. Null for payments in functional currency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.fiscal_period IS 'The fiscal period (month or quarter) within the fiscal year in which this payment was recorded. Used for period-based financial reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.fiscal_year IS 'The fiscal year in which this payment was recorded, based on the payment date. Used for financial period reporting and year-end closing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.functional_currency_amount IS 'The payment amount converted to the agency''s functional currency using the exchange rate. Used for consolidated financial reporting and P&L (Profit and Loss) analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.is_reversal IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether this payment is a reversal of a previous payment transaction. True if this is a reversal entry, False otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.memo IS 'Free-text memo or notes field providing additional context about the payment. May include invoice references, campaign details, or special instructions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.payee_name IS 'The name of the party receiving the payment. For inbound payments, this is the agency entity. For outbound payments, this is the vendor, publisher, or supplier.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.payer_name IS 'The name of the party making the payment. For inbound payments, this is the client or advertiser. For outbound payments, this is the agency entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.payment_date IS 'The date on which the payment transaction was executed or received. This is the business event date for cash flow recognition.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.payment_method IS 'The financial instrument or mechanism used to execute the payment: ACH (Automated Clearing House), wire transfer, check, credit card, debit card, or electronic transfer.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.payment_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the payment: pending (initiated but not cleared), cleared (funds transferred), failed (transaction rejected), cancelled (voided before clearing), reversed (funds returned after clearing), or reconciled (matched to invoice/payable).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.payment_type IS 'Classification of the payment purpose: invoice payment (standard settlement), advance payment (prepayment), refund (return of funds), rebate (volume discount payment), commission (agency fee), or retainer (upfront fee).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.reconciliation_date IS 'The date on which the payment was successfully reconciled to its corresponding invoice or bank statement. Null if not yet reconciled.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.reconciliation_status IS 'Indicates whether the payment has been matched to its corresponding invoice, payable, or bank statement entry: unreconciled (no match), partially reconciled (partial match), fully reconciled (complete match), or disputed (discrepancy identified).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.reference_number IS 'Externally-known unique reference number assigned to this payment transaction for tracking and reconciliation purposes. Used in bank statements and remittance advice.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.remittance_advice_reference IS 'Reference number or identifier from the remittance advice document accompanying the payment. Used to match payment to specific invoices or line items.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.sap_payment_document_number IS 'The payment document number generated in SAP S/4HANA FI module. Primary reference for integration with the ERP (Enterprise Resource Planning) system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.terms IS 'The contractual payment terms applicable to this payment (e.g., Net 30, Net 60, 2/10 Net 30). Indicates the agreed-upon payment schedule and any early payment discounts.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.value_date IS 'The date on which the funds become available in the receiving account or are debited from the paying account. Used for cash position and liquidity management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.withholding_tax_amount IS 'The amount of tax withheld from the payment as required by tax regulations. Common for cross-border payments and vendor payments subject to withholding.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.payment.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE finance.revenue_recognition IS 'Records governing when and how agency revenue is recognized from client contracts, retainers, and project-based engagements per ASC 606 / IFRS 15 standards. Captures contract reference, performance obligation description, recognition method (straight-line, milestone, percentage-of-completion), recognition start/end date, total contract value, recognized amount to date, deferred revenue amount, recognition status, fiscal period, and SAP FI revenue recognition document reference. Critical for accurate P&L reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.revenue_recognition_id IS 'Unique identifier for the revenue recognition record. Primary key for this entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the client (advertiser) for whom revenue is being recognized. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.agency_relationship_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.agency_relationship. Business justification: Revenue recognition in advertising agencies is governed by the fee structure of the agency relationship (retainer, commission, project). Linking revenue_recognition to agency_relationship supports rel LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.agency_relationship.agency_relationship_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.agreement_id IS 'Reference to the client contract or Statement of Work (SOW) that governs this revenue recognition event. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.agreement.agreement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: ASC 606 / IFRS 15 revenue recognition in advertising agencies is performed at the brand level as the performance obligation unit. Brand-level revenue recognition reporting is a standard finance requir LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the advertising campaign associated with this revenue recognition, if applicable. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.client_invoice_id IS 'Reference to the client invoice associated with this revenue recognition event, if revenue has been billed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Revenue recognition is attributed to cost centers for P&L reporting. Adding cost_center_id FK replaces natural key reference.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.delivery_pacing_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.delivery_pacing. Business justification: ASC 606 percentage-of-completion revenue recognition requires delivery milestone data. Linking revenue_recognition to delivery_pacing supports delivery-based revenue recognition calculations and audit LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.delivery_pacing.delivery_pacing_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Revenue recognition records post to specific GL revenue accounts. Adding gl_account_id FK replaces natural key reference.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_insertion_order. Business justification: Revenue recognized against insertion orders for agency commission and service fees - fundamental revenue accounting in advertising. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_insertion_order.media_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.media_placement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_placement. Business justification: Granular ASC 606 revenue recognition at placement level is required when each placement represents a distinct performance obligation. Agency finance teams recognize revenue as placements deliver; this LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_placement.media_placement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.milestone_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.milestone. Business justification: ASC 606/IFRS 15 revenue recognition in advertising agencies is tied to project milestone completion (performance obligations). revenue_recognition has denormalized milestone_name and milestone_date pl LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.milestone.milestone_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.performance_kpi_target_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.performance_kpi_target. Business justification: Revenue recognition for performance contracts depends on meeting KPI targets; ASC 606 performance obligations require target linkage. LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.performance_kpi_target.performance_kpi_target_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.plan_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan. Business justification: Revenue recognition for media agency services is tied to media plan delivery milestones under ASC 606 percentage-of-completion method. Linking revenue recognition to the media plan enables plan-level LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.plan.plan_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.adjustment_reason IS 'Explanation for any adjustment, reversal, or correction made to the revenue recognition record. Required when recognition status is adjusted or reversed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.approved_by IS 'User ID or name of the finance manager or controller who approved this revenue recognition entry, ensuring compliance with ASC 606 and internal controls.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.approved_timestamp IS 'Timestamp when this revenue recognition entry was approved by the finance manager or controller.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.contract_reference_number IS 'External business identifier for the contract or Statement of Work (SOW) document.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary amounts in this revenue recognition record (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.deferred_revenue_amount IS 'Amount of revenue that has been billed or received but not yet recognized, representing the contract liability. Calculated as total contract value minus recognized amount to date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.fiscal_period IS 'Fiscal period (month or quarter) within the fiscal year when revenue is recognized, typically 1-12 for monthly periods or 1-4 for quarterly periods.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.fiscal_quarter IS 'Fiscal quarter (1-4) within the fiscal year for quarterly business review (QBR) and financial reporting purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.fiscal_year IS 'Fiscal year in which this revenue recognition event occurs, used for financial reporting and Profit and Loss (P&L) aggregation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.is_active IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether this revenue recognition record is currently active (True) or has been superseded or voided (False). Used for soft deletes and historical tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.notes IS 'Additional notes, comments, or context regarding this revenue recognition event, including any special considerations or exceptions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.percentage_complete IS 'Percentage of completion for this performance obligation, used when recognition method is percentage-of-completion. Value between 0.00 and 100.00.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.performance_obligation_description IS 'Detailed description of the specific performance obligation being fulfilled (e.g., media planning services, creative production, campaign execution, retainer services).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.profit_center_code IS 'Profit center code in SAP S/4HANA CO for segment reporting and Earnings Before Interest Taxes Depreciation and Amortization (EBITDA) tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.recognition_end_date IS 'Date when revenue recognition is expected to complete for this performance obligation, typically aligned with contract end date or service completion.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.recognition_method IS 'Method used to recognize revenue for this performance obligation per accounting standards. Straight-line for retainers, milestone for project-based, percentage-of-completion for long-term campaigns, point-in-time for discrete deliverables.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.recognition_start_date IS 'Date when revenue recognition begins for this performance obligation, typically aligned with contract effective date or service commencement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.recognition_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the revenue recognition record. Pending indicates not yet started, in-progress for ongoing recognition, completed when fully recognized, deferred for postponed recognition, reversed for corrections, adjusted for amendments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.recognized_amount_to_date IS 'Cumulative revenue amount recognized to date for this performance obligation. Updated as revenue is recognized over time or at point in time.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.revenue_type IS 'Classification of revenue stream type. Retainer for ongoing monthly fees, project for fixed-price engagements, commission for percentage-based fees, media markup for agency margin on media buys, production for creative services, consulting for advisory services, performance fee for outcome-based compensation. Code set: ref.revenue_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.sap_fi_document_number IS 'SAP S/4HANA FI document number for the revenue recognition posting, providing traceability to the general ledger entry.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.sap_fi_posting_date IS 'Date when the revenue recognition entry was posted in SAP S/4HANA FI general ledger.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.service_line IS 'Agency service line or business unit delivering the performance obligation (e.g., Media Planning, Creative Services, Digital Marketing, Account Management, Data Analytics).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.total_contract_value IS 'Total monetary value allocated to this specific performance obligation from the contract. Represents the transaction price allocated per ASC 606 Step 4.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.unbilled_revenue_amount IS 'Amount of revenue recognized but not yet billed to the client, representing a contract asset or accrued revenue.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.revenue_recognition.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE finance.vendor_payable IS 'Accounts payable records for amounts owed by the agency to media vendors, publishers, production suppliers, freelancers, and technology partners. Captures vendor reference, payable document number, invoice date, due date, payment terms (net 30/60/90/120), gross amount, net amount, early payment discount amount, discount deadline, currency, payment status (open, scheduled, paid, disputed), SAP FI vendor invoice document number, Mediaocean Prisma payable reference, media buy reference, sequential liability flag, and reconciliation status. Supports media cost reconciliation, vendor payment processing, cash flow planning, and sequential liability management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.vendor_payable_id IS 'Unique identifier for the vendor payable record. Primary key for the vendor payable entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the client account for which this vendor expense was incurred. Supports client-level profitability analysis and budget tracking. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Vendor payables for media buys and production are attributed to specific client brands for brand-level cost of goods reporting and profitability analysis. vendor_payable has advertiser_id but brand-le LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.budget_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.budget_line. Business justification: A vendor payable represents the actual AP liability incurred against a planned budget line. Linking vendor_payable.budget_line_id -> budget_line.budget_line_id enables direct committed-vs-actual spend';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.buy_id IS 'Reference to the media buy that generated this vendor payable. Links the financial liability to the underlying media purchase for campaign cost tracking and Return on Ad Spend (ROAS) analysis. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.buy.buy_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the advertising campaign for which this vendor cost was incurred. Enables campaign-level margin analysis and Return on Investment (ROI) calculation. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: Media IOs create vendor payables when media is delivered; finance reconciles payables against IO terms for three-way match and payment authorization. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Vendor payables are attributed to cost centers for expense tracking. Adding cost_center_id FK replaces natural key reference.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.delivery_pacing_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.delivery_pacing. Business justification: Finance teams validate vendor payables against actual delivery pacing data before approving payment. This delivery-to-payable validation is a standard media finance reconciliation step ensuring vendor LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.delivery_pacing.delivery_pacing_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Vendor payables post to GL accounts (typically accounts payable liability accounts). Adding gl_account_id FK replaces natural key reference.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.io_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.io_line. Business justification: In advertising AP workflows, a vendor payable is generated against the specific IO line that authorized the spend. This enables 3-way match (IO line → delivery → payable) and is standard practice for';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.media_placement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_placement. Business justification: Payables reference specific placements for detailed cost tracking and delivery-based payment verification in vendor reconciliation. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_placement.media_placement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.performance_kpi_target_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.performance_kpi_target. Business justification: Performance-based vendor contracts include KPI-contingent payment terms. Linking vendor_payable to performance_kpi_target supports pay-for-performance payment processing and audit trails for KPI-gated LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.performance_kpi_target.performance_kpi_target_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.plan_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan_line. Business justification: Vendor payables should reference plan lines for planned-vs-actual cost reconciliation at the line level. Agency finance teams require this link to produce budget variance reports by media channel and LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.plan_line.plan_line_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.production_job_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.production_job. Business justification: Vendor payables (freelancers, studios, post-production) are tied to specific production jobs. Links payables to jobs for job costing, vendor cost reconciliation, and production budget variance analysi LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.production_job.production_job_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.reconciliation_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.reconciliation. Business justification: Advertising AP teams release vendor payments only after reconciliation confirms delivery. Linking vendor_payable to the reconciliation record that validated delivery is the core AP release workflow an';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.schedule_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.schedule. Business justification: Broadcast vendor payables are generated from schedule entries representing aired spots. Linking vendor payables to schedules enables affidavit-based billing verification — a standard broadcast media a LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.schedule.schedule_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.supplier_id IS 'Reference to the vendor, publisher, production supplier, freelancer, or technology partner to whom payment is owed. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.vendor_invoice_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.invoice. Business justification: Vendor payables track liabilities for specific vendor invoices. Finance teams reconcile payables against vendor.invoice records for payment matching, dispute resolution, and three-way match (PO-invoic';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.vendor_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.vendor_rate_card. Business justification: Vendor payable amounts are validated against the contracted rate card during AP processing. Advertising finance teams perform rate card verification as part of invoice approval — linking payable to ra LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.vendor_rate_card.vendor_rate_card_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.video_completion_event_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.video_completion_event. Business justification: Video vendor payables reconcile against delivered completions; CPCV payment validation requires completion event evidence. LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.video_completion_event.video_completion_event_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.viewability_measurement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.viewability_measurement. Business justification: Viewability-guaranteed vendor contracts pay only for viewable impressions; payable validation requires viewability measurement evidence. LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.viewability_measurement.viewability_measurement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.work_package_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.work_package. Business justification: Vendor payables for production work (video production, photography, studio time) are incurred against specific WBS work packages. Finance needs to match vendor costs to the work package for project co LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.work_package.work_package_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.approval_date IS 'The date the vendor payable was approved for payment. Marks the transition from pending review to authorized for payment processing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.approved_by IS 'The user identifier of the person who approved the vendor payable for payment. Required for financial controls and audit trail compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the payable amount (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP). Required for multi-currency financial reporting and foreign exchange management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.discount_amount IS 'The discount amount available if payment is made by the early payment discount deadline. Supports cash management optimization through early payment incentives.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.discount_deadline IS 'The last date by which payment must be made to qualify for the early payment discount. Used for cash flow optimization decisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.dispute_date IS 'The date the payable was flagged as disputed. Used for aging analysis of unresolved disputes and vendor relationship management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.dispute_reason IS 'Free-text description of the reason for disputing the vendor payable. Populated when payment_status is disputed. Used for vendor negotiation and dispute tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.due_date IS 'The date by which payment must be made to the vendor according to the agreed payment terms. Used for cash flow planning and aging analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.fiscal_period IS 'The fiscal period (month or quarter) within the fiscal year in which this vendor payable is recorded. Used for period-based financial reporting and variance analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.fiscal_year IS 'The fiscal year in which this vendor payable is recorded for financial reporting purposes. Derived from posting date and fiscal calendar configuration.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.gross_amount IS 'The total amount owed to the vendor before any discounts or adjustments are applied. Represents the full invoice value.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.invoice_date IS 'The date the vendor invoice was issued. This is the principal business event timestamp for the payable transaction and serves as the baseline for payment term calculations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.mediaocean_payable_reference IS 'The unique payable reference identifier from Mediaocean Prisma billing system. Enables reconciliation between media buying platform and financial system for media cost tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.net_amount IS 'The final amount payable to the vendor after applying early payment discounts and any other adjustments. This is the actual payment amount.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.notes IS 'Free-text notes or comments related to the vendor payable. Used for documenting special payment instructions, reconciliation notes, or other relevant information.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.payable_document_number IS 'The unique business document number assigned to this accounts payable record, used for tracking and reconciliation purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.payment_date IS 'The date the payment was actually made to the vendor. Null for unpaid payables. Used for cash flow reporting and payment performance analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.payment_method IS 'The payment instrument or mechanism used to settle the vendor payable. ACH (Automated Clearing House) for electronic bank transfers, wire transfer for same-day payments, check for paper-based payments, credit card for card-based payments, EFT (Electronic Funds Transfer) for direct bank transfers, virtual card for single-use card payments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.payment_reference_number IS 'The unique reference number assigned to the payment transaction (e.g., check number, wire confirmation number, ACH trace number). Used for payment tracking and bank reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.payment_status IS 'Current status of the vendor payment in the accounts payable lifecycle. Open indicates unpaid liability, scheduled indicates payment is queued, paid indicates payment completed, disputed indicates vendor dispute in progress, cancelled indicates payable voided, on_hold indicates payment temporarily suspended.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.payment_terms IS 'The contractual payment terms agreed with the vendor, typically expressed as net days (net_30, net_60, net_90, net_120). Determines the due date calculation from invoice date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.posting_date IS 'The date the vendor payable was posted to the general ledger. Determines the accounting period for financial reporting and may differ from invoice date for period-end accruals.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.reconciliation_status IS 'Status of the three-way reconciliation process between vendor invoice, media buy order, and actual delivery. Pending indicates awaiting reconciliation, matched indicates full agreement, discrepancy indicates variance requiring investigation, resolved indicates discrepancy closed, escalated indicates dispute requiring management intervention.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.sap_fi_document_number IS 'The SAP S/4HANA FI document number for the vendor invoice posting. Links the payable to the general ledger entry and enables full financial audit trail.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.sequential_liability_flag IS 'Indicates whether this payable is subject to sequential liability rules, where the agency is liable for vendor payment only after receiving payment from the client. Critical for cash flow management and risk mitigation in media buying.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.tax_amount IS 'The total tax amount included in the vendor payable (e.g., sales tax, VAT, GST). Required for tax reporting and compliance with jurisdictional tax regulations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.withholding_tax_amount IS 'The amount of tax withheld from the vendor payment as required by tax regulations. Reduces the net payment amount and must be remitted to tax authorities.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN finance.vendor_payable.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';
